prompt-caching-demo (examples/demos/prompt-caching/graph.yaml): Demonstrates Anthropic prompt caching with system_segments
prompt-theme-analyzer (examples/demos/prompt_theme_analyzer/graph.yaml): Read prompt files, classify concise themes with map fan-out, aggregate deterministically in Python, then group themes and write a markdown report. (FR-402)
promptfoo-tone-router-demo (examples/demos/promptfoo-router/graph.yaml): Route responses based on detected message tone
python-map-demo (examples/demos/python-map/graph.yaml): Demonstrates type:python sub-nodes in map nodes (FR-021)
python-variables-demo (examples/demos/python-variables/graph.yaml): Python node with declarative variable mapping from state
race-demo (examples/demos/race/graph.yaml): Race multiple LLM providers for the fastest response. Task shapes: same question to multiple providers or models, take the fastest good answer (hedging).
ramp_doctrine (examples/demos/ramp_doctrine/graph.yaml): FR-866 ramp doctrine draft — tailor this repo's Scripture traps, cures, and questions into a target-repo AGENTS.md draft. Deterministic collection feeds one map judgement per doctrine entry; code reconciles ids and writes draft artifacts only under tmp/ramp.
ramp_incidents (examples/demos/ramp_incidents/graph.yaml): FR-866 RAMP incidents — scan this repo's feature-request and diary corpus for target-repo mentions, classify each mentioned document as an operational incident or reconciliation-only non-incident, and write draft artifacts under tmp/ramp for target doctrine repatriation.
ramp_rtm (examples/demos/ramp_rtm/graph.yaml): FR-866 RAMP RTM — derive proposed requirement candidates from a target repository's existing test suite. Collection is deterministic, one map branch reasons over one test file, and the merge writes an honest draft with validation errors and unwitnessed-test gaps preserved.
recap (examples/demos/recap/graph.yaml): Timeframe change recap for any git repository — deterministic git collection, one synthesis judgement
reflexion-demo (examples/demos/reflexion/graph.yaml): Self-improving essay with critique loop
req-cross-check (examples/demos/req-cross-check/graph.yaml): Run architecture cross-check and produce traceability report (FR-107)
req-witness-audit (examples/demos/req_witness_audit/graph.yaml): Grade requirement-witness batches with a haiku-tier LLM and write one raw structured result per input batch for deterministic reconciliation.
research-agent (examples/demos/research-agent/graph.yaml): 5-step agentic research: extract intent, plan approach, execute research with tools, validate findings, synthesize report.
research-route (examples/demos/research-route/graph.yaml): FR-890 closed-input alternatives route: load a problem brief, collect known graph task shapes, fan out to orthogonal planner personas, and reduce their findings into a deterministic alternatives table.
tone-router-demo (examples/demos/router/graph.yaml): Route responses based on detected message tone. Task shapes: classify an input, then dispatch to a specialized handler (conditional routing).
router-race-candidates-demo (examples/demos/router-race-candidates/graph.yaml): Router node with candidates race support
run-analyzer (examples/demos/run-analyzer/graph.yaml): Analyze a previous run for issues and provide recommendations
safety-guards-demo (examples/demos/safety-guards/graph.yaml): Shows how YAMLGraph protects against unbounded execution: a draft→review→revise cycle (loop-guarded), then a map fan-out (item-capped), all under a recursion_limit.
salvage_classify (examples/demos/salvage_classify/graph.yaml): FR-868 scripture-dev salvage classifier — collect every tracked source file, classify each against this repository's committed equivalents, and write a human-review disposition draft under tmp/ramp.
self-portrait (examples/demos/self-portrait/graph.yaml): Local PersonalizationPortrait extraction with exact-payload consent before agent-first synthesis.
enforcer-workflow (examples/demos/session-continuation/graph.yaml): Two-phase development workflow using Copilot session continuation. Phase 1 (Enforce): Implement feature with TDD - failing test first, minimal change, refactor. Phase 2 (Demo): Create example and demo in examples/ folder using same session context.
session-shapes (examples/demos/session-shapes/graph.yaml): FR-884 session task-shape classifier: load session skeleton JSONL, classify each session with map fan-out, and aggregate shape coverage deterministically.
shared-vision-tool-demo (examples/demos/shared-vision-tool/graph.yaml): Minimal demo for the shared image description tool.
soul-pattern-demo (examples/demos/soul/graph.yaml): Demonstrates the soul pattern for AI agent personality
streaming-demo (examples/demos/streaming/graph.yaml): Two-node pipeline demonstrating token-by-token streaming. Run with: yamlgraph graph run graph.yaml --var topic="..." --stream
subgraph-demo (examples/demos/subgraph/graph.yaml): Demo of subgraph composition - parent graph calls a summarizer subgraph
system-status (examples/demos/system-status/graph.yaml): Gather system metrics with shell tools, then LLM diagnoses issues
tavily-rag (examples/demos/tavily_rag/graph.yaml): Domain-scoped RAG using Tavily as retrieval layer
thinking-demo (examples/demos/thinking/graph.yaml): Demonstrate extended thinking with configurable reasoning depth (FR-071)
tool-call-demo (examples/demos/tool-call/graph.yaml): Demonstrates tool_call node type — dynamic tool dispatch from state
typescript-node-json-demo (examples/demos/typescript-node/graph.yaml): Deterministic python-node graph for TypeScript subprocess integration
verification-demo (examples/demos/verification/graph.yaml): Node guards on a side-effect node plus a graph-wide verify block
verification-gate-demo (examples/demos/verification-gate/graph.yaml): Demonstrates the verification gate pattern (FR-164). Each node states what it expects; the framework checks after execution.
verified-search (examples/demos/verified-search/graph.yaml): POC: Evaluation-first agent pattern. The agent must state a verification question BEFORE taking action. The report extracts this question as structured output for traceability. This enables: - Post-hoc evaluation: Did the agent answer the question it claimed to ask? - LangSmith traces labeled with stated intent - Comparison of stated vs actual behavior Key insight: The verification_question is in the PROMPT (reasoning pattern), not the GRAPH (orchestration). Prompts define how to think; graphs define where data flows.
web-research (examples/demos/web-research/graph.yaml): Agent that researches topics using web search
wiki-memory-gate (examples/demos/wiki-memory/graph.yaml): Wiki page editor with reference-integrity gate
write-data-file-demo (examples/demos/write_data_file/graph.yaml): Accumulating world bible via read-compress-write cycle
yamlgraph-demo (examples/demos/yamlgraph/graph.yaml): Content generation pipeline (generate → analyze → summarize)
changelog-req-cross-check (graphs/enforcement/changelog-req-check.yaml):
fr_triage (.chaplain/graphs/fr_triage/graph.yaml): Canon pass + pre-mortem witnesses + value-prop check, appended into the FR as dispositionable claims
philosopher-scan (.chaplain/graphs/philosopher/graph.yaml): Scan diary entries for recurring patterns and propose graduations. Nine phases: scan → analyze → distill → unwrap_distill → [challenge → unwrap_challenge →] propose → load_context → reflect → write_diary. The distill/challenge gate (FR-195) prevents weak patterns from reaching .chaplain/inbox/.
