  os_infra_finding: {'persona': 'os-infra-primitivist', 'candidate': 'Enforce finding cell length ceiling via deterministic stdlib string-length check at artifact gate, rejecting any cell exceeding 400 characters before LLM scoring. Platform already provides byte-count primitives; no model needed.', 'solution_class': 'boundary-enforcement', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'CAP-17 Execution Safety Guards, CAP-56 Verification Gate Pattern, FR-598 kill-the-novel failure mode cited in incidents', 'is_this_a_graph': 'no', 'effort_risk': 'low/medium. Stdlib string length check is trivial; risk is ensuring gate runs before any scoring or row retention, blocking the whole artifact on first violation.', 'rationale': 'The witnessed 2000-character prose cells violate the stated 40-word, 400-character hard cap. A deterministic deny-path gate (CAP-17, CAP-56 pattern) at artifact assembly time prevents over-length rows from reaching the judge, closing the FR-598 reappearance without LLM involvement.'}
  data_process_finding: {'persona': 'data-process-planner', 'candidate': 'Strip author-supplied instrument names from brief constraints; require all persona context to come from committed repository state only.', 'solution_class': 'schema-data', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'FR-890 witnessed incident 2026-08-26: corpus_census, philosopher graph, and diary_index named in brief constraints seeded convergence; CAP-237 Author Brief Pre-Flight enforces shape validation before persona dispatch.', 'is_this_a_graph': "No. This is a schema and intake gate change: remove instrument/capability names from the brief's constraints section before any persona sees it, forcing discovery from committed state only.", 'effort_risk': 'Low effort, medium risk. Parsing and redaction are deterministic stdlib. Risk: authors may resist losing the ability to hint at solutions; mitigation is clear doctrine that hints defeat the closure boundary.', 'rationale': 'The witnessed echo (FR-893) proves that naming instruments in the brief contaminates persona independence. Removing those names at intake—before personas are spawned—dissolves the problem at the boundary rather than asking personas to ignore seeded context.'}
  yamlgraph_native_finding: {'persona': 'yamlgraph-native-planner', 'candidate': 'Enforce field length ceiling (400 chars hard cap) at schema validation time, not post-hoc. Reject any finding cell exceeding the limit before artifact assembly, forcing brevity into the closure boundary itself rather than relying on persona discipline.', 'solution_class': 'schema-data', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'CAP-207 Loader Error UX — schema validation failures surface early; FR-890 constraints require deterministic stdlib enforcement in deny path; witnessed incident 2026-08-26 (FR-890 D-9) shows schema gates work when applied.', 'is_this_a_graph': 'none: this is a schema/validation rule, not a graph orchestration task. No fan-out, no LLM reasoning, no state flow — pure deterministic gate.', 'effort_risk': 'Low. Add maxLength: 400 to finding cell schema fields (candidate, rationale, effort_risk, etc.). Reject at load time. No LLM, no new graph shape needed.', 'rationale': 'FR-890 constraints demand deterministic stdlib enforcement; witnessed 2026-08-26 incident shows 2000-char cells violate read-first discipline. Schema validation is the closure boundary — moving the ceiling there prevents over-length prose from entering the artifact at all.'}
  subtractionist_finding: {'persona': 'subtractionist', 'candidate': 'Delete the four-string author-brief context window entirely. Personas receive only committed repository state: capability registry, architecture headings, and Scripture keys. The brief supplies the FR number and incident list only; all problem framing comes from repository artifacts.', 'solution_class': 'boundary-enforcement', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'CAP-237 Author Brief Pre-Flight; Scripture key: one_session_one_repo, where_is_the_repo_boundary, instruction_boundary_uncrossed', 'is_this_a_graph': "No. This is a context-isolation enforcement rule, not a graph dependency. The change is structural: rewrite the persona invocation harness to strip the brief's constraints and incidents before dispatch.", 'effort_risk': 'Low. The harness already separates brief parsing from persona context assembly. Remove four string assignments; add a validation gate that rejects any persona context not sourced from committed state. Risk: none if gate is deterministic stdlib.', 'rationale': "FR-893 and FR-890 D-9 show that author framing in the brief contaminates convergence signal and enables echo-as-discovery. Removing the brief's constraints and incidents sections from persona context eliminates the seeding mechanism entirely. Personas then converge only on repository-committed facts, making convergence genuine independent discovery."}
  librarian_research: Search results for 'registered reports pre-specification research methodology preventing HARKing':

1. (PDF) Pre-registration and registered reports
   URL: https://www.researchgate.net/publication/343080321_Pre-registration_and_registered_reports
   Pre-registration and more strongly registered reports are expected to. reduce reporting and publication bias because they request researchers to define a detailed. research plan before the data are collected and before the research outcome is known.

2. Pre-Analysis Plans in R: Commit Before You Analyze
   URL: https://r-statistics.co/Pre-Analysis-Plans-in-R.html
   A pre-analysis plan is a public commitment to your research design, hypotheses, and analysis approach — written and registered before you look at the data. It's the single most effective tool against p-hacking, HARKing, and the garden of forking paths.

3. Pre-Registration: Why It Matters | MetricGate
   URL: https://metricgate.com/blogs/pre-registration-why-it-matters/
   Registered Reports take pre-registration one step further by embedding it into the peer-review process. Authors submit their introduction and methods — including the pre-registration — before collecting data.

4. 60th Online Seminar: Preregistration
   URL: https://gfzpublic.gfz.de/rest/items/item_5007840_2/component/file_5007841/content
   In pre-registration, researchers describe their hypotheses, methods, and analyses before a piece of research is conducted, in a way that can be externally verified. Registration prioritizes theory, analysis and methods over results.

5. Should You Pre-Register Your Research Study? - Enago Academy
   URL: https://www.enago.com/academy/pre-registration-of-your-research/
   Pre-registration also prevents HARKing, or “hypothesizing after results are known.”The Pros and Cons of Pre-Registering Your Research. Pre-registration has benefits for you as a researcher. It guarantees clarity among collaborators and prevents accusations of p-hacking.

  librarian_tool_results: [{'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'multi-persona independent discovery convergence signal contaminated context research methodology', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'multi-persona independent discovery convergence signal contaminated context research methodology':\n\n1. Multiple discovery - Wikipedia\n   URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multiple_discovery\n   The concept of multiple discovery is the hypothesis that most scientific discoveries and inventions are made independently and more or less simultaneously by multiple scientists and inventors.\n\n2. Your AI Is Getting Dumber: How to Fix Context Poisoning in... | Medium\n   URL: https://medium.com/no-time/your-ai-is-getting-dumber-how-to-fix-context-poisoning-in-your-2026-workflow-2d156919ab1a\n   Long-context research, prompt injection research, and homogenization research all point in the same direction: quality falls when the model loses a clean distinction between signal and noise, instruction and data, voice and default. So here is the rule worth keeping on your desk\n\n3. Signal Contamination — ShodhDynamics AI Discovery Lexicon\n   URL: https://shodhdynamics.com/ai-discovery-lexicon/signal-contamination/\n   Signal Contamination requires displacement. The negative associations already exist. They are strongly encoded, reinforced by repetition, corroborated across multiple independent sources — which is exactly the kind of signal AI systems weight most heavily.\n\n4. Convergence Discovery Methodology | Multi-System Verification\n   URL: https://cetianji.app/studio/blog/studio-crossverify-convergence-methodology\n   The **Convergence Discovery Methodology** offers a structured, repeatable approach to moving from independent readings across different systems to a unified, actionable conclusion.\n\n5. Research Methods - Types, Examples and Guide\n   URL: https://researchmethod.net/researchmethods/\n   Research Methods refer to the techniques, procedures, and processes used by researchers to collect, analyze, and interpret data in...\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'blind review process independent expert panels avoiding confirmation bias', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'blind review process independent expert panels avoiding confirmation bias':\n\n1. Avoiding Confirmation Bias in Marketing Research\n   URL: https://www.linkedin.com/advice/0/youre-analyzing-marketing-research-data-how-yizqc\n   How can you avoid confirmation bias affecting your decisions? Powered by AI and the LinkedIn community.Confirmation bias, the tendency to interpret new evidence as confirmation of one's existing beliefs or theories, can be a significant obstacle in marketing research.\n\n2. Confirmation Bias In Psychology: Definition & Examples\n   URL: https://www.simplypsychology.org/confirmation-bias.html\n   Confirmation Bias is the tendency to look for information that supports, rather than rejects, one’s preconceptions, typically by interpreting evidence to confirm existing beliefs while rejecting or ignoring any conflicting data.\n\n3. Confirmation bias in science: how to avoid it - Ars Technica\n   URL: https://arstechnica.com/science/2010/07/confirmation-bias-how-to-avoid-it/\n   Confirmation bias is remarkably common—it is used by psychics, mediums, mentalists, and homeopaths, just to name a few. As you may guess from such a list, deliberate use of confirmation bias is held in low esteem by scientists...\n\n4. 6 Biases That Can Affect Our Designs | by Coumba Win | Medium\n   URL: https://medium.com/@coumbawin/6-biases-affect-designs-7f1db1b3342c\n   The bias blind spot seems to be a genuine blind spot, in that it is not actually related to our ability to make decisions. Regardless of their actual decision making ability, people tend to believe that they are less biased than others. Final thoughts.\n\n5. Confirmation Bias in Business & How To Avoid It - Growth Idea Ltd\n   URL: https://growthidea.co.uk/blog/confirmation-bias-in-business-how-to-avoid-it\n   When it comes to confirmation bias, business leaders need to be especially careful.The interview process and hiring process: A manager might interview a job candidate and only ask them questions that confirm their cognitive bias that the candidate is qualified for the job.\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'Delphi method expert consensus avoiding groupthink contamination', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'Delphi method expert consensus avoiding groupthink contamination':\n\n1. Delphi method - Wikipedia\n   URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delphi_method\n   The following key characteristics of the Delphi method help the participants to focus on the issues at hand and separate Delphi from other methodologies: in this technique a panel of experts is drawn from both inside and outside the organisation.\n\n2. The Delphi Technique: How to Predict Business Risks... - Insight Ginie\n   URL: https://insightginie.com/the-delphi-technique-how-to-predict-business-risks-without-groupthink/\n   Learn how the Delphi Technique uses anonymous expert feedback to identify risks and build consensus without the noise of groupthink.\n\n3. Delphi Method Summary and Forum - 12manage\n   URL: https://www.12manage.com/methods_helmer_delphi_method.html\n   Strengths of the Delphi Method. Benefits. Rapid consensus. Participants can reside anywhere in the world. Coverage of wide range of expertise. Avoids Groupthink. Forecasting a specific, single-dimension question. Limitations of the Delphi Method.\n\n4. Groupthink | Examples & Avoidance - Expert Program Management\n   URL: https://expertprogrammanagement.com/2011/03/groupthink-examples-avoidance/\n   Groupthink is particularly prevalent in cohesive groups, groups with a strong leader, and groups working in isolation. A number of general techniques exist to avoid groupthink, along with a number of specific tools, including Nominal Group Technique and The Delphi Method.\n\n5. How to Use the Delphi Method for Problem-Solving\n   URL: https://www.linkedin.com/advice/3/how-can-you-use-delphi-method-reach-consensus\n   It can help you avoid groupthink, bias, and conflicts that may arise from direct discussions or debates. In this article, you will learn how to use the Delphi Method to solve a problem in six steps.\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'blind review methodology independent verification context isolation research', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'blind review methodology independent verification context isolation research':\n\n1. Scientists Reveal Hidden World Below the Pyramids - Independent...\n   URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gDcPBPx0Fv8\n   Two independent research teams have discovered matching underground structures beneath Egypt's Giza plateau, extending over 1.2 kilometers deep, deeper than three Empire State Buildings stacked.\n\n2. Data Verification - Definition, Methods, Process, and Examples\n   URL: https://researchmethod.net/data-verification/\n   Data verification versus research validity. Types and Methods of Data Verification.Two research assistants independently enter the responses. Software compares both datasets and produces a discrepancy file. Each discrepancy is resolved by returning to the original questionnaire.\n\n3. From Inertia to Objectivity: Improving Deep Research Agents with...\n   URL: https://arxiv.org/html/2608.23045\n   We propose the Noise Isolation Search Agent (NIS-Agent), a multi-agent framework for open-web deep research.Beyond these isolation-specific cases, the large majority of remaining failures fall into four categories that are largely independent of context isolation.\n\n4. Find the Best Prop Firms in 2026 | Verified Reviews... | TheTrustedProp\n   URL: https://thetrustedprop.com/\n   We've researched, reviewed, and ranked 400+ prop firms to help you compare prop trading firms and avoid falling into trading scams.\n\n5. Peer Reviewed Video Platform for Scientific Research and... | JoVE\n   URL: https://www.jove.com/\n   Explore JoVE, the peer-reviewed video platform with 30,000+ lab method and science concept videos. Trusted by 1,800+ universities and companies worldwide.\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'pre-registration research design preventing p-hacking confirmation bias', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'pre-registration research design preventing p-hacking confirmation bias':\n\n1. Research Preregistration 101 – Association for Psychological...\n   URL: https://www.psychologicalscience.org/observer/research-preregistration-101\n   A: Yes. Preregistration helps honest researchers do good work, but it is not designed to prevent fraud (although it may make it harder). Q: Are there other advantages to preregistering? A: Preregistration can make your research more efficient.\n\n2. Preregistration in psychology\n   URL: https://nrin.nl/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/PhD-dissertation-Olmo-van-den-Akker.pdf\n   Similarly, preregistration helps prevent p-hacking by demanding researchers to explicitly specify research decisions before data collection.\n\n3. Confirmation Bias in Personalization | acceleroi\n   URL: https://www.acceleroi.com/blog/confirmation-bias-personalization\n   Pre-registration prevents most cherry-picking.P-hacking is the statistical mechanism through which confirmation bias produces false positives — running multiple analyses (segments, metrics, time windows) and reporting only the one that confirms the desired result.\n\n4. Pre-registering prompts is an interesting idea. I don’t think I’d do that...\n   URL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/scott-cunningham-7788912_pre-registering-prompts-is-an-interesting-activity-7463915523148378112-yYPL\n   I argue for another one, which seems to be helpful, at least to some extent, in addressing p-hacking: pre-registration. Researchers should preregister their prompts before running their simulations.\n\n5. (PDF) Questionable research practices following pre-registration\n   URL: https://www.academia.edu/121084405/Questionable_research_practices_following_pre_registration\n   The pre-registration system is recommended by many psychologists as well as journals in other fields to prevent QRPs, as it functions as a platform that is used before the start of a study. Researchers can register a detailed plan of their study design and upload data continuously...\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': '"closed input" research methodology artifact verification schema', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': 'Search results for \'"closed input" research methodology artifact verification schema\':\n\n1. ASE 2026 - Research Papers - ASE 2026\n   URL: https://conf.researchr.org/track/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track\n   The ASE conference is the premier research forum for Automated Software Engineering. Each year, it brings together researchers and practitioners from academia and industry to discuss foundations, techniques, and tools for automating the analysis, design, implementation, testing, and maintenance of large software systems.\n\n2. Papers with Code — Trending research and open source\n   URL: https://paperswithcode.co/\n   Trending AI research papers with code, datasets, methods, and evaluation leaderboards.\n\n3. An Auditable LLM-RAG Architecture for Financial Document ...\n   URL: https://www.mdpi.com/1999-5903/18/6/284\n   May 26, 2026 · The research gap addressed in this work is therefore not the absence of a single retrieval model, reranker, or LLM, but the lack of a reproducible methodology that connects retrieval, grounded generation, structured validation, numerical consistency, and persistent audit artifacts into one financial document workflow.\n\n4. The TEVV-Athlon Framework for Evaluating AI Systems - ipd\n   URL: https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/ai/NIST.AI.200-2.ipd.pdf\n   AI 422 evaluation can involve technical, scientific, and human-centered methods drawn from ar-423 eas such as computer science, signal detection theory, experimental design, psychology, 424 statistics, and quantitative and qualitative social science research.\n\n5. ACL ARR 2026 May | OpenReview\n   URL: https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org/ACL/ARR/2026/May\n   ReViz: Structured Visual Synthesis of Research Methodology Diagrams ACL ARR 2026 May Submission17420 Authors 26 May 2026 (modified: 02 Jul 2026) ACL ARR 2026 May Submission Readers: Everyone 0 Replies Show details\n', 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'multi-rater agreement inter-rater reliability independent judges convergence', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'multi-rater agreement inter-rater reliability independent judges convergence':\n\n1. Using Differential Item Functioning to Test for Inter-rater Reliability in...\n   URL: https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/217187463.pdf\n   Inter-rater reliability and agreement indices rooted in classical test theory were presented.The traditional inter-rater agreement indices that were examined in this study did not exhibit as high of power raters as did the DIF statistic derived from a nested design, βNe.\n\n2. Statistical inference for indices of interrater agreement based on...\n   URL: https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10260-026-00846-z\n   Statistical Methods for Inter-Rater Reliability Assessments.Interrater agreement is influenced by both the characteristics of the raters as well as of the targets being evaluated. Raters homogeneity implies that raters apply the same standards in the evaluation process.\n\n3. stata - Calculation for inter-rater reliability where raters don't overlap....\n   URL: https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/180970/calculation-for-inter-rater-reliability-where-raters-dont-overlap-and+-different\n   How to perform inter-rater reliability with multiple raters, different raters per participant, and possible changes over time?\n\n4. Inter-Rater Agreement | Envisioning Vocab\n   URL: https://www.envisioning.com/vocab/inter-rater-agreement\n   Inter-rater agreement quantifies how consistently multiple human evaluators assign the same labels or judgments to the same data points.High inter-rater agreement in evaluation protocols strengthens the credibility of benchmarks and safety assessments alike.\n\n5. rater-agreement · PyPI\n   URL: https://pypi.org/project/rater-agreement/\n   Chance-corrected agreement statistics for any raters, human or model — kappa, weighted kappa, Fleiss, Krippendorff's alpha, ICC, intra-rater reliability, kappa-paradox diagnostics, with bootstrap CIs.\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'adversarial collaboration independent teams research design avoiding echo chamber', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'adversarial collaboration independent teams research design avoiding echo chamber':\n\n1. (PDF) Keep Your Enemies Close: Adversarial Collaborations Will...\n   URL: https://www.researchgate.net/publication/356944598_Keep_your_enemies_close_Adversarial_collaborations_will_improve_behavioral_science\n   adversarial collaborations to avoid investments in counterproductive research areas.Some teams have sustained adversarial collaborations for years. One team in Germany. has focused on studies testing theories of consciousness (Melloni et al., 2021).\n\n2. The Adversarial Collaboration Method for Research and Scholarship\n   URL: https://heterodoxacademy.org/resources/the-adversarial-collaboration-method-for-research-and-scholarship/?trk=public_post_comment-text\n   Adversarial collaborations bring together teams of intellectual “adversaries” to tackle contested research questions within shared areas of expertise.\n\n3. Adversarial Collaboration | Springer Nature Link\n   URL: https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-04968-2_16\n   Adversarial collaboration is an approach to resolving scientific disputes, wherein researchers who have different positions on the issue at hand collaborate with the aim of making progress on their disputed research question.\n\n4. Adversarial Collaboration Project | Adversarial Collaboration...\n   URL: https://web.sas.upenn.edu/adcollabproject/\n   Research Team. Advisory Board. Participate.Adversarial Collaboration Project. 3720 Walnut St University of Pennsylvania Philadelphia, PA 19104. Email: adcollabproject@sas.upenn.edu.\n\n5. Adversarial Collaboration (Dispute Protocol) — AI Alignment Forum\n   URL: https://www.alignmentforum.org/w/adversarial-collaboration-dispute-protocol\n   Adversarial collaboration is a protocol developed by Daniel Kahneman for two researchers advocating competing hypotheses to collaborate on a research project with the goal of resolving their differences...\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'registered reports pre-specification research methodology preventing HARKing', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'registered reports pre-specification research methodology preventing HARKing':\n\n1. (PDF) Pre-registration and registered reports\n   URL: https://www.researchgate.net/publication/343080321_Pre-registration_and_registered_reports\n   Pre-registration and more strongly registered reports are expected to. reduce reporting and publication bias because they request researchers to define a detailed. research plan before the data are collected and before the research outcome is known.\n\n2. Pre-Analysis Plans in R: Commit Before You Analyze\n   URL: https://r-statistics.co/Pre-Analysis-Plans-in-R.html\n   A pre-analysis plan is a public commitment to your research design, hypotheses, and analysis approach — written and registered before you look at the data. It's the single most effective tool against p-hacking, HARKing, and the garden of forking paths.\n\n3. Pre-Registration: Why It Matters | MetricGate\n   URL: https://metricgate.com/blogs/pre-registration-why-it-matters/\n   Registered Reports take pre-registration one step further by embedding it into the peer-review process. Authors submit their introduction and methods — including the pre-registration — before collecting data.\n\n4. 60th Online Seminar: Preregistration\n   URL: https://gfzpublic.gfz.de/rest/items/item_5007840_2/component/file_5007841/content\n   In pre-registration, researchers describe their hypotheses, methods, and analyses before a piece of research is conducted, in a way that can be externally verified. Registration prioritizes theory, analysis and methods over results.\n\n5. Should You Pre-Register Your Research Study? - Enago Academy\n   URL: https://www.enago.com/academy/pre-registration-of-your-research/\n   Pre-registration also prevents HARKing, or “hypothesizing after results are known.”The Pros and Cons of Pre-Registering Your Research. Pre-registration has benefits for you as a researcher. It guarantees clarity among collaborators and prevents accusations of p-hacking.\n", 'success': True}]
  librarian_finding: {'persona': 'librarian', 'candidate': 'Registered Reports embed pre-specification into peer review: authors submit introduction and methods—including pre-registered hypotheses—before data collection, preventing HARKing and p-hacking by locking analysis plans before outcomes are known.', 'solution_class': 'external-method', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'https://www.researchgate.net/publication/343080321_Pre-registration_and_registered_reports', 'is_this_a_graph': 'No. Registered Reports is a peer-review workflow, not a graph structure. It enforces temporal ordering (specification before data) and role separation (reviewers see methods before results).', 'effort_risk': 'Medium. Requires upfront specification discipline and review-gate enforcement, but uses standard academic infrastructure. Risk: authors may resist pre-commitment; mitigation is clear incentive alignment.', 'rationale': "FR-890's core failure is that author-supplied context (brief constraints) contaminates persona independence, producing echo-chamber convergence. Registered Reports solve this by enforcing specification closure before observation—personas would commit analysis plans before seeing any results, making convergence signal genuine discovery rather than brief-echo."}
